module Task.Internal exposing (Task)

{-| The type of a `Task`, in a module `core` does not expose
(`m1b-source.md` §SO11, after D233's `Bytes.Transient` and D240's
`Array.Transient`).

It was declared in `Platform`, which close-out item 4 deleted (§SO19). It could
not move into `Task` while `Platform.sendToApp` answered a `Task` and `Task`'s
own effect manager named `Platform.Router`, since the two modules would have
imported each other, and a third module both could import was the answer the
two transients gave to the same problem. `Source` and `Extern` build tasks
without being `Task`, so the type stays here.

A `Task` has no constructor that Geng can reach. Its nodes are built by the
`task_` primitives, which `Task` declares, and run by the backend's scheduler
(D246, `m1b-source.md` §SO24).

-}


{-| A description of something to do, which does nothing until it is run.
-}
type Task err ok
    = Task
